  nonce: c75d  # c75d
  message: "SATISFIED by PR #200 (5ad8a7a6bb). Behavioural evidence, the item's own filed\nrepros re-run on merged dev:\n\n  REPRO 1 -- in-repo callee\n    raw module slot   'src/app/views.py'\n    normalizer        'src/app/views'\n    LOOKUP KEY        'src/app/views.handler'   (was 'src/app/views.py.handler')\n\n  REPRO 2 -- python logging entries\n    _qualified_callee(\"python:logging:0-0:info:external_symbol\") -> 'logging.info'\n    'logging.info' in catalogue        -> True   (was False)\n    'logging.Logger.info' in catalogue -> True   (kept, see below)\n\n  CONTROLS -- every key the shipped catalogues actually declare is external,\n  so these are the load-bearing half:\n    fmt.Printf             -> 'fmt.Printf'             OK\n    net/http.Get           -> 'net/http.Get'           OK\n    go.uber.org/zap.String -> 'go.uber.org/zap.String' OK\n    unresolved placeholder -> ''  (was the fiction 'external.print')\n\nEFFECT ON THE SECTION 4 NUMBERS: DERIVABLY ZERO, not re-measured, and that is\na considered choice rather than a shortcut. The shipped catalogues declare only\nstdlib and third-party names, so an in-repo key still matches nothing.\nMeasured on a self-survey (141,494 edges, 72,822 call-like, 6,685 distinct\ncallees): the key changes for 5,981 distinct callees / 64,177 call-edge\ninstances, and catalogue hits are 0 before and 0 after. Running a 16-minute\ncohort A/B to rediscover a null derivable from five lines of the consumer is\nexactly what L59 was minted for. The re-measurement that IS owed belongs after\nthe variable-identity fix, which changes the substrate underneath all of it.\n\nFACET 2 RESOLVED ON MEASUREMENT, not on the filing's guess. Across 64\nlogger-method call sites the module slots present are `warnings` (51),\n`external` (12) and one file path -- NOT ONE carries `logging.Logger`, so the\nfiling's suspicion was right and is now confirmed rather than assumed.\nBare-module logging.* entries added; the Logger-qualified ones KEPT (correct,\nnever consulted while unmatched, and they fire if receiver resolution ever\nimproves) with the split documented in the YAML instead of left as silent dead\ndata.\n\nFACET 3 NOT DONE, stated rather than implied. The qualified-key filter still\ndrops 44 of 113 loaded keys with no log line. The filter is correct and\ndeliberate; the silent 40% drop is a diagnostic gap, not a defect in the key,\nso it is outside this invariant's statement. Not filed separately -- it is a\none-line disclosure whoever next touches the loader should add.\n\nNEW LIMITATION INTRODUCED BY THIS FIX, filed separately rather than buried\nhere: stripping the extension removes an accidental barrier, so an in-repo path\ncan now normalise onto a stdlib module key (net/http.go -> net/http). 42 of 69\nshipped qualified keys are shadowable in principle; zero collisions across the\n72,822 measured call edges. A false \"terminates\" CLOSES a branch, which deletes\nfindings, so this is the expensive direction. Latent while section 3a is\nconfirm-only."  # c75d
